Batman will always definitely be the  hero we deserve but after headlining 10  films in the past three decades he's not  the hero we need right now let's take a  look at all the other Batman characters  who deserve their own movies if you want  a villain who's begging for a solo movie  clayface's origin story is basically  already the plot to an amazing horror  film the original version is set around  the filming of a slasher movie called  Dredd Castle but whenever it's time to  film a death scene suddenly the lights  go out and the actor playing the victim  mysteriously dies for real those who  catch glimpses of the fleeing killer see  that he looks like Clayface a famous  fictional monster from another old  horror film eventually Batman intervenes  and discovers that the Clayface Killer  is actually a horror actor makeup artist  vassal Carlo who played both the movie  monster Clayface and the killer in the  original Dredd Castle Carlo claims he  committed the murders because he didn't  want anyone replacing him as Dredd  castles killer he apparently played so  many fictional monsters that it turned  him into a real-life horror movie  villain a version of this story with or  without Batman could be an awesome  horror flick like scream 7 the 40's and  since he can look like anyone there's no  guarantee that they got the right guy  how's that for a third act twist usually  the only Batman villains who make it to  the big screen are the truly threatening  a list masterminds like the Joker and  Ra's al Ghul that's all well and good  but a wonderful thing about Batman is  that he has so many villains that go  beyond just the household names Gotham  has an extremely deep roster of b-list  baddies so we'd be remiss if we didn't  include at least one of Batman's miner  more comedic enemies ok are you making  some of those up nope they're all real  somewhere far down towards the bottom of  the roster you'll find an obscure Batman  villain known as the eraser his real  name is Lenny Fiasco and he's our pick  for a point of view character in the  world of Batman's many Forgotten foes  the eraser has found an interesting  niche in Gotham's criminal underworld  and that he works as a fixer for other  villains helping them erase the evidence  of their crimes in exchange for a 20  percent cut  a film centered on the eraser could be a  low-stakes crime comedy along the lines  of The Big Lebowski whenever another  Batman villain Boches one of their  supervillain plots the eraser ash I put  upon everyman dons his giant pencil  costume and does his best to clean  things up how great would it be to see  the working-class side of super villainy  with cameo appearances from the  different Batman villains who need to  call upon the eraser services we've had  many different actors play Batman over  the years but every cinematic version of  Batman has been Bruce Wayne underneath  the cape and cowl the 2009 comic by  Grant Morrison and Frank Quitely simply  entitled Batman and Robin however could  be adapted pretty much directly into an  excellent film about someone trying to  fill Bruce Wayne's big black boots when  the story opens Bruce Wayne has been  killed by Darkseid and Dick Grayson the  first Robin who had more recently been  the hero Nightwing decides to take over  the role of the Dark Knight to keep  things safe in Gotham City he also takes  on Damian Wayne Bruce's son with Talia  al Ghul as his Robin because Damian was  raised by an order of assassins without  ever knowing his father he grew up  rebellious arrogant and violent and he  has no respect for dick as his partner  needless to say dick and Damian's first  few missions didn't go particularly well  at one point dick tells Alfred that he  feels like a kid doing a Batman voice  and that it was foolish to even try to  replace Bruce Wayne after Alfred  encourages him to treat the identity of  Batman as a performance in which he's  playing a role dick stops trying to be  Bruce Wayne and he learns to be Batman  in his own way and after Damian's  recklessness almost gets him killed and  dick asked to save him he starts to  realize that maybe this new Batman  actually knows what he's doing  perhaps no single Batman character has  had a wider array of comic-book  portrayals than Pamela Isley better  known to Gotham City by her highly  evocative plant-based criminal code name  poisoned poison ivy  she's been everything from a thief to an  eco-terrorist to a superhero in her own  right with powers that range from being  a nearly normal human with an immunity  to toxins and a serious knack for  gardening to a living avatar of plant  life itself who can take over the entire  world with hypnotic spores it might seem  like that inconsistency could hurt her  as a character but really it just means  that there are a lot of different  options when it comes to bringing her to  film including putting them all together  in one it would be easy enough to tell a  story that followed the example of a  movie like Captain Marvel where Pamela's  control of her plant powers would slowly  ramp up over the course of the film  there's even an option to show her as  more than just a costumed criminal but  as a defender of a planet in dire need  of help against very relevant issues  like climate change she could even work  in the absence of Batman by pitting her  against bad guys like Jason Woodrum sure  they already did that in Batman and  Robin but it's not like anyone would  notice plus her romantic relationship  with Harley Quinn has made her a fan  favorite giving her a ready-made  connection to the current run of DC  movies one which Harley Quinn actress  Margot Robbie says she wants to explore  on screen there are a lot of origin  stories about bad guys who learn to be  good but what about one where a good guy  turns bad there are numerous versions of  mr. Freeze's origin story but typically  Victor fries who's actually a doctor not  a mister is a brilliant scientist whose  wife Nora contracts a terminal illness  freeze searches for a cure and in order  to buy himself some time to look he puts  her into cryonics stasis later an  accident in the cryonics lab alters  Victor's body chemistry leaving him  unable to live outside a sub-zero  environment  he turns to crime to fund his  increasingly expensive research not to  mention his presumably massive  air-conditioning bills so he makes a  freeze gun and starts stealing stuff  beneath all the wonderful campy nonsense  the tragedy of mr. freeze holds a  surprisingly touching message about love  and more  ality because of Victor's unwillingness  to accept his wife's impending death he  ends up squandering both their lives  trying in vain to change her destiny  when he should have just enjoyed what  time he and Nora had left together  fleeting though it might be or to put  another way  after a dire diagnosis a brilliant yet  cash-strapped scientists invents a  criminal alter-ego to help get money for  his family it's basically everything you  like about Breaking Bad except that  instead of making meth like Walter White  Victor fries invented a freeze gun and  started fighting Batman while making ice  puns Gotham central began in 2002 as a  comic book series with an interesting  hook it's a law-and-order style police  procedural set in Gotham City with an  ensemble cast focusing on the normal  people who try to keep law and order in  a city dominated by superheroes and  deadly costumed villains during its  forty issue run it was a critical  darling and features a number of stories  that could be adapted into an excellent  new our detective movie perhaps the most  famous story from Gotham central was  half a life in which two-face puts into  motion an elaborate plan to destroy the  life of Renee Montoya one of Gotham's  best detectives by hiring someone to  outer as a lesbian it then turns out  that this is just step one of his plan  giving Montoya a motive because later  two-face murders the person he hired and  frames Montoya for it Montoya ends up in  jail and the rest of her colleagues on  the GCPD need to catch two-face and  clear their colleagues name another way  to go would be a story like dead Robin  which is a fascinating look into how the  criminal justice system of Gotham  intersects with the world of superheroes  in this tale Gotham police find the dead  body of a teenage boy in a Robin costume  with no identification they're not sure  if he's the real Robin or just a kid  dressed up like him but they have to  attempt to identify the body and figure  out who killed him while navigating a  world of secret identities it's an  excellent hook for a murder mystery and  it only gets better from there  you think we'd have seen a Batgirl movie  by now Joss Whedon was writing one for a  while but has since left claiming he  didn't have a story currently Christina  Hudson  the writer of bumblebee is attached to a  potential film but potential is all it  has right now as the project still lacks  a director  maybe the reason it's taking so long is  because Barbara Gordon's history is more  than a little complicated here's the  quick version  she was Batgirl she got paralyzed by the  Joker so she became Oracle a super  hacker information broker for  superheroes some readers like this  because it was cool to see a disabled  superhero but some didn't because they  thought she never should have been  paralyzed in The Killing Joke to begin  with then Barbara's paralysis went away  and thanks to the universe being  rebooted she became Batgirl once more  and again some readers like this and  some didn't with all of that to deal  with how do you make a movie about  Batgirl you could make a dual timeline  story with some scenes taking place  during Barbara's days as Batgirl and  others during her time as Oracle then  again maybe it would be better to tell a  breezy continuity light story and not  mention the paralysis at all but that  would mean ignoring almost 30 years of  her history and some very important  representation it's a tough problem to  crack but if anyone deserves to have the  effort put in its Barbara Gordon if you  haven't heard a cat man we don't blame  you from his earliest appearance in the  1960s  he's been mostly just a punch line  between a costume that's goofy even by  Silver Age DC standards and his use of  Catering's cat man has the somewhat  unique distinction of being a fictional  character who's accused in universe of  being a ripoff of  other much cooler characters although he  languished in obscurity for decades cat  man came back in the mid 2000s in the  pages of secret six a sort of spiritual  successor to Suicide Squad but without  the part where they were working for the  good guys instead this was the story of  a type of super team that hasn't been  seen much in the movie so far  super mercenaries the secret six are  superhuman muscle for hire and as such  their morality is somewhat flexible  perhaps the six is most film worthy  Adventure occurs when they gain  possession of a mystical item known as a  get out of hell free card  the name implies it's a little metal  rectangle that allows its bearer to  rescue anyone's soul from hell and  return them to the world of the living  needless to say once it becomes widely  known that the secret six possesses this  every supervillain in the world starts  coming for them a film adaptation about  Cat Man and the rest of the six during  this time could be a madcap guardians of  the galaxy style dirty action comedy  with a heart of gold  sure cat man might be a dumb name but  come on is it any worse than star-lord  simply put Batman Beyond is one of the  greatest superhero cartoons of all time  it takes place in a futuristic cyberpunk  Gotham where Bruce Wayne is retired from  his life as Batman and now he's a bitter  jaded shuttin inner Terry McGinnis a  rebellious teenager with a good heart  who accidentally discovers the secret  identity of Batman when Terry's father  is then murdered Terry steals a bat suit  from Bruce Wayne and sets out to bring  his father's killer to justice  although Bruce tries to stop him at  first once he realizes that Terry is a  good kid with pure intentions he decides  to take Terry under his pointy cape and  serves as the guy in the chair doing  research and giving him advice there's  so much to love about the idea of a  Batman Beyond movie franchise the  cyberpunk setting would look gorgeous in  live-action and there's an entirely new  rogues gallery of creepy villains like  inked blight Spellbinder and more and  you know what Michael Keaton is just  about the right age nowadays to play a  retired Bruce Wayne just saying check  out one of our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite stuff are coming soon subscribe  to our YouTube channel and hit the bell  so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

